  666 f34d:             ;
  667 f34d:             ; O command: boot. Read the boot block (LBA 0) to OSBASE, check 'P8' and OSCNT, read OSCNT sectors from LBA 1
  668 f34d:             ; to OSBASE and call it; the OS returns with RET.
  669 f34d:             ;
  670 f34d:             ;
  671 f34d:             ; ':' - Intel-hex loader (YACC1-D 2026-09-23). A ':' at the prompt starts load mode: the rest of the record is read
  672 f34d:             ; without echo (uartinne), its bytes stored from its address on, and the record acknowledged with one character:
  673 f34d:             ;   .  stored and the checksum is right
  674 f34d:             ;   ?  a bad hex digit or a bad checksum
  675 f34d:             ;   !  refused or not verified: an address outside $1000-$DFFF (the monitor's page, the stack and the ROM are
  676 f34d:             ;      protected; any write to $E000-$FFFF would reach the 28C64, review M2), or the byte read back differently
  677 f34d:             ; Between records everything up to the next ':' is skipped (CR, LF, blanks), so an assembler .img can be pasted into
  678 f34d:             ; a terminal or sent as is; ESC (or a NUL, the emulators' end of input) abandons, between records or inside one. The end record (type 01) prints
  679 f34d:             ; LOADED, or LOADED WITH ERRORS when any record failed, and returns to the prompt. Records of other types are read
  680 f34d:             ; and checked but not stored. Host side: tools/monload.py paces the characters (the UART has no FIFO enabled: one
  681 f34d:             ; character of buffering) and waits for each acknowledgement. Registers: R3 checksum, R4 count, R5 type,
  682 f34d:             ; R6 record status (0 ok, 1 bad hex, 2 refused/unverified), R7 the address; never R2.
  683 f34d:             ;
  684 f34d:             hexload:
  685 f34d: 0d 05               LDTI  LOADMODE
  686 f34f: e7 0f 00            STT   monmode
  687 f352: 0d 00               LDTI  0
  688 f354: e7 0f 01            STT   lderr
  689 f357:             ldrec:
  690 f357: 1b 00 00            MVIW  R3,0
  691 f35a: 1c 00 00            MVIW  R4,0
  692 f35d: 1e 00 00            MVIW  R6,0
  693 f360: 04 f4 08            JSR   ldbyte            ; byte count
  694 f363: 34                  MVARL R4
  695 f364: 04 f4 08            JSR   ldbyte            ; address high
  696 f367: 3f                  MVARH R7
  697 f368: 04 f4 08            JSR   ldbyte            ; address low
  698 f36b: 37                  MVARL R7
  699 f36c: 04 f4 08            JSR   ldbyte            ; record type
  700 f36f: 35                  MVARL R5
