 1712 fa19:             ;
 1713 fa19:             ; OLD: Output null terminated string pointed to by R2 to UART then send CR and LF
 1714 fa19:             ; Advances R2 to end of string
 1715 fa19:             ;
 1716 fa19:             ; Output null terminated string pointed to by R7 to UART
 1717 fa19:             ; Advances R7 to end of string
 1718 fa19:             ;
 1719 fa19:             stringout:
 1720 fa19: 09                  Push
 1721 fa1a:             sloop:
 1722 fa1a: 47                  LDAVR R7
 1723 fa1b: a1 fa 25            BRZ sloopdone
 1724 fa1e: 04 fa 27            JSR uartout
 1725 fa21: 57                  INCR R7
 1726 fa22: a0 fa 1a            BR sloop
 1727 fa25:             ;
 1728 fa25:             ; (not done send CR and LF)
 1729 fa25:             ;
 1730 fa25:             sloopdone:
 1731 fa25: 0a                  POP
 1732 fa26: 05                  RET
 1733 fa27:             ;
 1734 fa27:             ; output accumulator to UART, wait for UART out available
 1735 fa27:             ;
 1736 fa27:             charout:
 1737 fa27:             uartout:
 1738 fa27:             ;
 1739 fa27:             ; 2026-09-25: the video mirror. With VIDMIR and VIDPRES set the byte also goes to the screen (vputc, which keeps
 1740 fa27:             ; every register and TMP); with VIDMIR 0 this costs a PUSH, an LDA, a BRZ and a POP, and the UART path below is as
 1741 fa27:             ; it was. ACC, TMP and R3-R7 are kept either way (R2 is LDA's address register, as in every LDA).
 1742 fa27:             ;
 1743 fa27: 09                  PUSH
 1744 fa28: e4 0f f1            LDA VIDMIR
 1745 fa2b: a1 fa 3b            BRZ chnovid
 1746 fa2e: e4 0f f0            LDA VIDPRES
 1747 fa31: b1 01               SUBI 1                  ; 2026-10-22: VIDPRES exactly 1 (vprobe writes 1 or 0): RAM never set by a reset
 1748 fa33: a2 fa 3b            BRNZ chnovid            ;   ($FF on the emulators) must not turn the mirror on with VCOLSV/VLINE garbage
 1749 fa36: 0a                  POP
 1750 fa37: 09                  PUSH
 1751 fa38: 04 f5 dc            JSR vputc
 1752 fa3b:             chnovid:
 1753 fa3b: 0a                  POP
 1754 fa3c:             ;
 1755 fa3c:             ; add for emulator, outputs via putch
 1756 fa3c:             ;
 1757 fa3c: af fa 41            BRDEV emulator2
 1758 fa3f: 62                  outa p2
 1759 fa40: 05                  ret
 1760 fa41:             ;
 1761 fa41:             emulator2:
 1762 fa41: 09                  PUSH
 1763 fa42: 09                  push
 1764 fa43:             ;
 1765 fa43:             ; doubt 2nd push pop is needed, to be tested
 1766 fa43:             ;
 1767 fa43:             uartoutw:
 1768 fa43:             ;
 1769 fa43:             ; test uart out is available
 1770 fa43:             ;
 1771 fa43: 70 68               OUTI  P0,(UARTCS!UARTA5)
 1772 fa45: 91                  INP   p1
 1773 fa46: b3 40               ANDI  040h
 1774 fa48: a1 fa 43            BRZ   uartoutw
 1775 fa4b: 0a                  POP
 1776 fa4c: 70 40               OUTI  P0,UARTCS
 1777 fa4e: 61                  OUTA  P1
 1778 fa4f:             ;
 1779 fa4f:             ; may not be needed
 1780 fa4f: 0a                 Pop
 1781 fa50: 05                 RET
 1782 fa51:             
 1783 fa51:             ;
 1784 fa51:             ; wait for UART character available then input to accumulator
 1785 fa51:             ;
 1786 fa51:             ; Looks like this echos out character
 1787 fa51:             ; should this be settable via a flag
 1788 fa51:             ;
 1789 fa51:             uartin:
 1790 fa51:             ;
 1791 fa51:             ; added for emulator, emulator P2 reads a char via getch
 1792 fa51:             ;
 1793 fa51: af fa 56            BRDEV emulator3
 1794 fa54: 92                  inp p2
 1795 fa55: 05                  ret
 1796 fa56:             ;
 1797 fa56:             emulator3:
 1798 fa56:             ;
 1799 fa56:             ; wait for a charater available at input (2026-11-10: the UART or the V2.0 card's keyboard, whichever has one)
 1800 fa56:             ;
 1801 fa56: 04 f3 3e            JSR   kbst
 1802 fa59: a1 fa 60            BRZ   uartwt
 1803 fa5c: 9e                  INP   PE
 1804 fa5d: a0 fa 6b            BR    uartcv
 1805 fa60: 70 68       uartwt: OUTI  P0,(UARTCS!UARTA5)
 1806 fa62: 91                  INP   p1
 1807 fa63: b3 01               ANDI  01h
 1808 fa65: a1 fa 56            BRZ   emulator3
 1809 fa68: 70 40               OUTI  P0,(UARTCS)
 1810 fa6a: 91                  INP   P1
 1811 fa6b: 0d 0d       uartcv: ldti 0dh          ; cobvert 0x0d to 0x0a
 1812 fa6d: aa fa 72            brneq uartinc
 1813 fa70: 0e 0a               ldai 0ah
 1814 fa72:             uartinc:
 1815 fa72: 04 fa 15            JSR   LEDOUT
 1816 fa75:             ;
 1817 fa75:             ; emulator
 1818 fa75:             ;
 1819 fa75:             ;        ldti  0ah
 1820 fa75:             ;        breq uartin
 1821 fa75: 04 fa 27            JSR   uartout
 1822 fa78: 05                  RET
 1823 fa79:             ;
 1824 fa79:             ; uartinne: uartin WITHOUT the echo and the LED (2026-09-23, vector $FFFC): Y1/OS's CONIN syscall reads the
 1825 fa79:             ; console for a program (a filter reading its input) and the shell echoes what it wants itself. Same paths:
 1826 fa79:             ; port 2 on the instruction-level emulator (BRDEV), the UART on the machine; CR becomes LF.
 1827 fa79:             ;
 1828 fa79:             uartinne:
 1829 fa79: af fa 7e            BRDEV uartinnehw
 1830 fa7c: 92                  inp p2
 1831 fa7d: 05                  ret
 1832 fa7e:             uartinnehw:
 1833 fa7e: 04 f3 3e            JSR   kbst              ; 2026-11-10: the V2.0 card's keyboard, else the UART
 1834 fa81: a1 fa 88            BRZ   uartinnew
 1835 fa84: 9e                  INP   PE
 1836 fa85: a0 fa 93            BR    uartinnecv
 1837 fa88:             uartinnew:
 1838 fa88: 70 68               OUTI  P0,(UARTCS!UARTA5)
 1839 fa8a: 91                  INP   p1
